Mask board clock spurs and the LO bin in the spectrum sent to clients

The receiver of a Pluto-class board picks up harmonics of its own clocks (25 MHz
and 100/3 MHz measured on a Fishball 7010) and the LO leaks through at the
centre bin, so the waterfall and spectrum show large spikes. The spectrometer
now replaces those narrow lines with the level of their surroundings before the
spectrum is sent to /waterfall clients, so the Maia UI, the Dashboard and the
classifier all see the masked data. IQ samples and recordings are not touched.

A line is masked only if it is within 50 ppm of a harmonic, stands 8 dB above its
surroundings and is at most 5 bins wide at half its height in dB (never measured
more than 10 dB below the peak, so strong lines with wide skirts are still
masked). Only for the AD9361 input. Creating /mnt/jffs2/no-spur-mask disables it.

